+// OpenGL 4.3 core / OpenGL ES 3.2 backend for plume.
+//
+// Design (docs/specs/backend-contract.md in TK64):
+// - One thread owns the GL context. Resource creation is run on it synchronously; command lists record closures on
+//   any thread and the queue replays them on the GL thread.
+// - Shaders arrive as SPIR-V and are translated to GLSL by tk64::translateSpirv when a pipeline is created, with one
+//   binding map shared by all stages of the pipeline.
+// - Rendering keeps D3D/Vulkan's memory layout (row 0 at the top): the SPIR-V vertex shaders already use Vulkan's
+//   inverted clip-space Y, and the translator remaps depth to GL's range, so viewports, scissors, copies and texture
+//   coordinates are passed through unchanged, and the swap chain flips the image when it is presented.
+// - The window belongs to the host. The context is WGL on Windows and EGL on Linux and Android. EGL and the GL
+//   client library are loaded at run time, so this file includes no EGL or GL headers outside Windows.
+//
